/// Editing a component's source through the edit service (P4 task 11). Unlike
/// `kai:app`, this is a granted interface (ADR 0003 section 3, like `kai:fs`
/// and `kai:net` later): only an app whose package holds the `edit` grant can
/// import it, the grant is shown when the package is installed, and a component
/// that imports it without the grant does not stage (`Reason::Link`). A request
/// is not run inside the call that makes it, as the app's other effects are not:
/// the host sends it after the call and tells the app the answer in a later one.
package kai:edit@0.1.0;

interface edit {
    /// Queues `message` for the edit service and returns its ticket. A message is
    /// `open <component> [<label>] [at <path>:<line>]` or `cmd <line>`, as the
    /// kernel's edit mode sends them; the answer is `ok ...` or `err ...` text.
    /// Traps when 16 messages already wait for the host (it sends them after each
    /// call into the app), or when `message` is empty or longer than 8,192 bytes.
    send: func(message: list<u8>) -> u32;
}

/// What the edit service answered.
interface replies {
    /// The answer to the message with this ticket, or why there is none (the
    /// service is not running, did not answer, or the message was not one an app
    /// may send). Tickets are not reused while the app runs.
    on-reply: func(ticket: u32, outcome: result<list<u8>, string>);
}

/// An app that edits source: the two halves of the grant.
world editing {
    import edit;
    export replies;
}
